  "published": "2026-08-12T00:34:46Z",
  "modified": "2026-08-12T00:34:46Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: netlogon secure channel allowed RC4/HMAC-MD5 downgrade\n     and unsealed (unencrypted) use, permitting man-in-the-middle attacks\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2022-38023.patch: change \"reject md5 clients\" and\n       \"reject md5 servers\" defaults to yes, deprecate \"allow nt4 crypto\" and\n       \"reject md5 clients\", add \"server schannel require seal\" (default yes)\n       and require DCERPC_AUTH_LEVEL_PRIVACY in the source3 and source4\n       netlogon servers including all netr_LogonSamLogon* variants, defer the\n       ServerAuthenticate3 downgrade check until the account is found in the\n       SAM so that \"server reject md5 schannel:COMPUTERACCOUNT\" and\n       \"allow nt4 crypto:COMPUTERACCOUNT\" exceptions apply\n     - CVE-2022-38023",
